messages:
eli: Quick pass on small screens today. On low-end Android the sidebar overlaps the table header and the header becomes sticky but unreadable when scrolled. Screenshot attached.
nina: Reproduced on a Moto G emulator. Looks like z-index + transform on the header is the culprit; header gets pushed under the sidebar when window < 400px.
ben: Two UX options: convert rows to stacked cards on very narrow viewports, or keep a condensed table with inline expand. Cards avoid horizontal clipping but increase vertical scroll.
clara: I prefer stacked cards at <=360px because they allow richer row actions to be visible without overflow. We can show primary metadata and a tappable chevron to reveal the rest.
eli: Also noticed the sidebar toggle overlaps the table's rightmost cells when opening; we should animate the content shift instead of overlaying so values don't get covered.
nina: For animations, prefer transform-based transitions to avoid layout jank. Also, disable scroll chaining on the sheet to avoid scrolling the background when the sheet is fully open.
ben: Copy nit: change mobile action button label from 'Details' to 'Open details' and menu item 'View on desktop' -> 'Open on desktop' for consistent verbs.
clara: Accessibility notes: stacked cards must preserve heading hierarchy (use role="heading" and level), ensure the expand button has aria-expanded and aria-controls, and set focus to the first interactive control inside the card when expanded.
a11y-bot: Checklist reminder: ensure 48px touch targets, focus restoration on close, aria-live region updates for dynamic list changes, and test TalkBack/VoiceOver. Reference: https://go/internal-mobile-a11y
eli: Implementation sketch:
```
@media (max-width: 360px) {
  .table { display: block; }
  .row { display: block; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .row .summary { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }
}
.row__expand[aria-expanded="true"] { background: var(--bg-elevated); }
```
nina: QA checklist for prototype: Moto G, Pixel 3a, iPhone 8 emulator; test with large text / zoom; test with VoiceOver/TalkBack; ensure no horizontal scrollbar.
ben: I'll prototype the stacked card layout + content-shift animation. Clara can own the ARIA attributes and copy updates.
clara: Yep, I'll do the a11y pass and update the copy. Targeting a short demo by Thursday.
eli: Great. I'll file the spec with breakpoints (<=360 card, 361-420 compact table, >420 full sidebar) and include the animation guidance. Tagging you all. :white_check_mark:
